<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>
  <!--
    Biotech module strings (src/Biotech/). Ten files contribute:
      - GeneInspectionPatch.cs    (Harmony patch, no user-facing text)
      - GeneInspectionState.cs    (baby/embryo/genepack/xenogerm gene tree)
      - GeneTreeBuilder.cs        (gene-tree node labels, biostats summary)
      - GrowthMomentPatch.cs      (Harmony patch, no user-facing text)
      - GrowthMomentState.cs      (child growth moment dialog: info/passions/traits)
      - MechControlGroupState.cs  (mechanitor control group settings/members)
      - XenogermPatch.cs          (Harmony patch, no user-facing text)
      - XenogermState.cs          (Dialog_CreateXenogerm tabbed tree)
      - XenotypeEditorPatch.cs    (Harmony patch, no user-facing text)
      - XenotypeEditorState.cs    (Dialog_CreateXenotype tabbed tree)

    Shared vocabulary (edge announcements, info-card unavailable, typeahead
    feedback, tree expansion state, level suffix) is sourced from
    RimWorldAccess_Common.xml. Gene names, xenotype labels, category labels,
    and all biostat terms (Complexity, Metabolism, Archites) come from the
    game's own vanilla translation keys via .Translate(), so they are NOT
    duplicated here.

    Placeholders follow string.Format ({0}, {1}, ...). One/Many variants exist
    where English needs singular/plural agreement (e.g. "1 gene" vs "N genes").
    Other languages can collapse or further split these using their own XML.
  -->

